/ llm-writer: a value put into an LLM message goes whole up to the max, a long list is cut with a marker and its columns named, and %x.trim% gives the same view.
/ This goal is the plan's index and its proof: each stage is a goal, each comment a behaviour we want,
/ and the step under it runs the test that proves it. Tests live under this plan's folder at the path of
/ what they test. The text is start.md; checks tests can't show are there too.
Start
- call Stage1
- call Stage2
- call Stage3
- call Stage4

Stage1
/ a short value goes into the message whole, as today
- call /plan/llm-writer/module/llm/ShortTextGoesWhole
/ a text over the max is cut, and the LLM is told how much more there was
- call /plan/llm-writer/module/llm/LongTextIsCutWithAMarker

Stage2
/ a list over 100 items: its columns and types first, then 100 rows, then "--- N more rows ---"
- call /plan/llm-writer/module/llm/LongListIsCutWithColumns
/ a dict gives its keys and their types
- call /plan/llm-writer/module/llm/DictGivesItsKeysAndTypes

Stage3
/ an image is described, never inlined
- call /plan/llm-writer/module/llm/ImageIsDescribed

Stage4
/ %x.trim% gives a list as the LLM would see it
- call /plan/llm-writer/app/type/list/TrimIsTheLlmView
/ a text's trim is its own, as today (a guard)
- call /plan/llm-writer/app/type/text/TextTrimIsAsBefore
